+    Business identifiers may be used in <code>Practitioner.identifier</code> and/or <code>Practitioner.qualification.identifier</code> based on local requirements.<br/>
+    A license or similar business identifier in <code>Practitioner.identifier</code> does not, by itself, convey qualification details such as status, issuer, or type; it can carry only the identifier's own period. When qualification details such as status or validity period are known or need to be exchanged, use <code>Practitioner.qualification</code> and its child elements; if qualification status is not known, omit <code>Practitioner.qualification.status</code>.<br/>
+    The same qualification can have multiple identifiers, such as one assigned by the certifying body and another assigned by an internal system. Jurisdictional or system profiles may constrain this cardinality when only one identifier is appropriate.<br/>
+    The Practitioner <code>identifier</code> search parameter includes both paths, so identifiers are searchable whether sent in either or both locations.
